<title>UK: Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs fall in week.</title>
<headline>Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs fall in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of active oil and gas rigs in operation offshore northwest Europe fell by four to 55 in the week to September 11, consultants Arthur Andersen said.</p>
<p>The Norwegian sector was unchanged with 14 rigs active, while the U.K. sector was down one at 29 and Denmark was down one at four.</p>
<p>The Dutch sector was down two rigs at seven, while Irish activity was unchanged at one.</p>
<p>Onshore drilling activity was unchanged at three rigs, two in the U.K. and one in the Faroe Islands.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4088</p>
</text>
